{
  "case_id": "2010-09-529",
  "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Virginia Office for Protection and Advocacy (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GALANTER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nThe Virginia Office for Protection and Advocacy, known as \"VOPA,\" seeks to enforce its Federal statutory right to inspect and copy records that are in the possession of State officials who run State-operated hospitals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But there are a number of instances in the States where constitutional officers have their separate autonomy, their separate responsibilities. And it seems to me to follow inevitably from your position that the attorney general of State A could sue the governor of State A saying the governor is being sued in an Ex parte Young capacity because the governor is not following Federal law. I think that's just inevitable from your -- from you position, and that seems to me a vast extension of Ex parte Young."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you think -- do you think the Spending Clause allows the Federal Government to condition the receipt of Federal funds on a State's agreement to change the structure of State government?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Ms. Anders, I understand that most States that -- that are taking advantage of this program do it through a private entity, not a State; is that -- is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Anders",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first choice was to opt into the DD and PAIMI Act programs, to take the Federal funds, to create a P and A system that has Federal rights of access to which both State and private facilities are subject."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Anders",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are eight public P and A systems."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Anders",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0001-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If Virginia were to dissolve VOPA, it would be out of compliance with the Federal scheme, and so it would lose its -- it would lose its Federal funding at that point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you be a little bit more specific for me on what you mean about an Article III problem?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Going back to your exchange with Justice Breyer, I assume that you could stand by your answer and say the attorney general could sue the governor, because he's not suing the governor in his official capacity. He has a Federal right under Ex parte Young to sue the governor as an individual."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Earle Duncan Getchell, Jr.",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0001-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF EARLE DUNCAN GETCHELL, JR., ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Earle Duncan Getchell, Jr.",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The dignity interest of a sovereign is impaired if it is pitted against itself in the courts of another sovereign without its consent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Earle Duncan Getchell, Jr.",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So if we're going to say it makes a difference under a spending statute that the State has taken the money in analyzing the sovereign interest, then we are creating a waiver on the cheap and disheveling the established doctrine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm asking you what is the forum? We have a simple problem. An agency, whether private or public, wants records."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "I would -- I personally believe you could also do it in circuit court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It hasn't happened. Why do you think? Don't you think it hasn't happened because there are so many practical political restraints on that kind of activity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you know -- do you know of any other statute in which there is an independent State agency that exists for the sole purpose of administering a Federal program?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "University of Massachusetts v. State Environmental Organization. Does that -- does that kind of suit sound familiar to you or -- or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0002-0010",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Virginia took a lot of money to set up and get the benefits of Federal funds by creating an independent agency. It had expressed its desire to control the agency more, and it was told very directly: You can't. You have to let that agency sue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.78,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0002-0011",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Congress, if you want Federal courts to be able to enforce the Federal right, then you have to set it up as an agency, as a private agency. You can't give -- Congress, you can't give the States a choice whether they'd rather do it through private or public organizations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So you -- you would acknowledge that if a State knew when it took the money that it was -- and when it created a State agency to administer the program, that it was letting itself open to suit in Federal court under an Ex parte Young theory, then everything would be okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "are there a lot, a few, none -- where one State agency at a State level sues another in Federal court, period?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fba5e9f02c7-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have one question of curiosity. You said in your opening argument that 49 of 50 States limit in some way the executive's power in this area."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-529",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "4fba5e9f02c74abc9866a3b0c8442c68f94ab40824811467cc7a3d51b4a57e00",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-4fba5e9f02c7-56",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
